# Exclusions for the Link check workflow (.github/workflows/link-check.yml).
# One regular expression per line. Every entry says why it is skipped.

# temporary — remove when the domain is reattached (dougdevitre.org is down:
# the hub's CNAME was deleted 2026-04-07).
^https?://(www\.)?dougdevitre\.org

# BROKEN — needs a human (found 2026-10-18). Returns 404 to the link checker
# (the Venmo button on about.html, the pillar pages and README.md). Could not
# confirm a working profile URL (venmo.com blocks automated fetches).
^https://venmo\.com/dougdevitre

# BROKEN — needs a human (found 2026-10-18). The Mailchimp signup form's POST
# action on about.html returns 404 to a GET. That may just be how the endpoint
# answers GETs, or the audience may be gone; a human needs to submit the form.
^https://us16\.list-manage\.com/subscribe/post\?u=62137ae349&id=090aae7d15

# Venmo donate link. venmo.com/u/dougdevitre opens Doug's profile in a browser
# (he confirmed it on his phone 2026-10-24), but Venmo answers automated
# checkers with 404, so lychee can't verify it. If the button ever breaks,
# check it by hand in a browser.
^https://venmo\.com/u/dougdevitre$
